# App ID String Safety

- Treat `appId` / app route `id` as `string` in frontend code.
- Do not convert app IDs to `Number` (`Number(...)`, unary `+`, `parseInt`) before API calls.
- When calling app APIs, pass ID as `string` (or `string | number` typed union), preferring string.
- Reason: backend uses Long IDs; JS number precision can corrupt IDs and cause "data not found".

## Examples

```ts
// bad
const appId = Number(route.params.id)
await getAppVoById({ id: appId })

// good
const appId = String(route.params.id || '')
await getAppVoById({ id: appId })
```
